WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:15.309
Unit six: Informal Messages and Notes. Today you will write short friendly messages and notes.

4
00:00:15.609 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.569
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.313
Informal.

7
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.291
Informal means relaxed and friendly in style.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:31.138
Use informal English with friends.

9
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.147
Your turn. Say: Informal.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.013
Informal.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.577
Note.

12
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.687
Note means a short written message.

13
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:44.877
Leave a note on the door.

14
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.822
Your turn. Say: Note.

15
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:51.586
Note.

16
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.502
Invitation.

17
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:57.341
Invitation means a request to come to an event.

18
00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.427
Thanks for the invitation.

19
00:01:00.017 --> 00:01:02.623
Your turn. Say: Invitation.

20
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:06.595
Invitation.

21
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.235
Cheers.

22
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.283
Cheers means an informal word for thanks or goodbye.

23
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:14.175
Cheers for your help!

24
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.366
Your turn. Say: Cheers.

25
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.062
Cheers.

26
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:22.899
Contraction.

27
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.754
Contraction means a short form like I'm or don't.

28
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.804
I'm is a contraction.

29
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.756
Your turn. Say: Contraction.

30
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.717
Contraction.

31
00:01:36.483 --> 00:01:37.322
Catch up.

32
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.804
Catch up means to talk after a long time.

33
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.917
Let's catch up soon.

34
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:45.786
Your turn. Say: Catch up.

35
00:01:48.633 --> 00:01:49.507
Catch up.

36
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.565
Apologise.

37
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.805
Apologise means to say sorry.

38
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:57.161
I apologise for being late.

39
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.472
Your turn. Say: Apologise.

40
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.543
Apologise.

41
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:06.331
Reminder.

42
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:10.036
Reminder means something that helps you remember.

43
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.394
Here is a quick reminder.

44
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:15.578
Your turn. Say: Reminder.

45
00:02:18.433 --> 00:02:19.539
Reminder.

46
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:24.042
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:27.707
Visal, how is an informal message different?

48
00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:36.299
It sounds friendly and relaxed. You can use contractions like I'm and don't, and short greetings like Hi or Hey.

49
00:02:37.383 --> 00:02:39.313
What do I write in an invitation?

50
00:02:40.417 --> 00:02:49.547
Say what the event is, when and where it is, and ask your friend to reply. For example, Do you want to come to my party on Saturday?

51
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.115
Can I use slang?

52
00:02:53.217 --> 00:03:00.583
A little with close friends, but keep it clear. Never use informal style in a letter to a boss or teacher.

53
00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:03.582
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.648
Grammar focus: Contractions.

55
00:03:06.948 --> 00:03:08.054
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.842
I'm having a party on Saturday.

57
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.332
We'll meet at six o'clock.

58
00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:19.253
Use contractions in informal writing: I'm, we'll, don't. Avoid them in formal writing.

59
00:03:20.017 --> 00:03:22.959
Be careful! Don't say: I am not know about it.

60
00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.109
Say: I don't know about it.

61
00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:28.665
Use don't with know.

62
00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.933
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:32.733 --> 00:03:34.036
A Note to a Friend.

64
00:03:34.336 --> 00:03:36.974
Chantha writes a note to her friend Sreyleak.

65
00:03:37.967 --> 00:03:41.000
She begins with Hi and uses contractions.

66
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.127
She says, I'm sorry I missed your call.

67
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.458
She invites her to a picnic on Sunday.

68
00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.559
She ends with See you soon and her name.

69
00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:55.726
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:58.432
An informal message is blank.

71
00:03:58.732 --> 00:04:02.234
A, friendly. B, strict. C, long.

72
00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.753
The answer is A: friendly.

73
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:10.069
I'm is a blank.

74
00:04:10.369 --> 00:04:13.685
A, date. B, contraction. C, title.

75
00:04:17.233 --> 00:04:19.244
The answer is B: contraction.

76
00:04:20.383 --> 00:04:22.894
An invitation asks someone to blank.

77
00:04:23.194 --> 00:04:26.336
A, leave. B, pay. C, come.

78
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.016
The answer is C: come.

79
00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.150
Apologise means to say blank.

80
00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.546
A, sorry. B, hello. C, no.

81
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.774
The answer is A: sorry.

82
00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.288
Chantha invites her friend to a blank.

83
00:04:47.588 --> 00:04:51.009
A, court. B, picnic. C, exam.

84
00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.555
The answer is B: picnic.

85
00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.976
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:01.817 --> 00:05:03.863
How do you write a friendly message?

87
00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.115
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:14.415 --> 00:05:23.816
I start with Hi and use contractions like I'm and don't. I keep it short and say clearly what, when and where. I end with See you soon.

89
00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:25.872
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:26.783 --> 00:05:30.666
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and contractions.

91
00:05:30.966 --> 00:05:35.186
Today's value is friendliness. Smile and say hello to everyone.

92
00:05:35.486 --> 00:05:37.895
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:05:38.195 --> 00:05:40.986
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

